293
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,280
I hate pickled tomatoes.

294
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:29,780
Pickled tomatoes, pickled pickles, pickled olives, everything.

295
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,960
I love it all.

296
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:35,060
I hate, I actually, there are a couple of things that I don't really like.

297
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:44,520
For example, coleslaw, you mentioned that it has cabbage in it and many people may know this vegetable as this purple lettuce, right?

298
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,240
It looks like a lettuce, but it's purple.

299
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:46,400
That's right.

300
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,240
I hate it.

301
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,240
I don't like it.

302
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,260
And I actually hate olives and pickles.

303
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:52,600
I can't really eat them.

304
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:56,440
Sounds like you don't like bitter things like vinegar, olives.

305
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:57,960
Yeah, yeah, no.

306
00:12:59,020 --> 00:12:59,280
Not a big fan.

307
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,600
I'm not a big fan of anything that's bitter.

308
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,280
I love it.

309
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,600
It's one of my favorite.

310
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:06,460
I love salty foods and I love bitter foods and that's all I have to say about it.

311
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:13,990
I've never really understood how people have like a whole pickle and they take it out of the jar and they just bite into it.

312
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,330
It's like, that's nasty.

313
00:13:15,590 --> 00:13:18,710
Well, the adjective to describe a pickle's flavor is sour.

314
00:13:19,110 --> 00:13:19,410
Sour.

315
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:20,330
It's very sour.

316
00:13:20,930 --> 00:13:25,610
And in America, at delis, you can buy full sours or half sours.

317
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:26,130
Oh, really?

318
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,070
Some pickles are less sour than others.

319
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:29,590
We call it a half sour.

320
00:13:30,010 --> 00:13:32,190
My favorite pickles are full sours.

321
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:32,790
Really?

322
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:35,840
Make you cry a little bit.

323
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,210
The whole pickle thing, is this very American?

324
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,190
Because you always have pickles in burgers, for example, right?

325
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,080
You go to McDonald's, you have pickles in burgers.

326
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:44,560
Is this very American or is this coming from another place?

327
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,810
It comes from Europe.

328
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:46,960
Oh, really?

329
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:50,690
A lot of German food involves pickles, pickled vegetables.

330
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:56,230
The Koreans also, Korean food has a lot of pickled vegetables like kimchi, which is pickled cabbage.

331
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,310
Oh, that's right.

332
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,160
And in Chinese culture as well, a lot of pickled foods.

333
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:02,410
So I think this is something that's very common all over the world.

334
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:04,050
You can have pickled fish.

335
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:05,430
Really?

336
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,600
Yeah.

337
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,230
You can pickle anything.

338
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,890
I don't know if we pickle things in Latin America.

339
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,890
This is why it seems very strange to me.

340
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:13,830
But this is a really interesting topic.

341
00:14:13,830 --> 00:14:16,530
Why don't you let us know what your favorite cured meats are?

342
00:14:16,650 --> 00:14:18,290
I know there are a lot of different types.

343
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:22,880
